2026-09-27T10:19:11.9312967Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9313242Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9313928Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9314347Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9314475Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9314794Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9314977Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9315217Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9315747Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9316095Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9316253Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9316661Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9316927Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9317118Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9317673Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9318192Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9319206Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9320116Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9320260Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9320957Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9321850Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9322317Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9322808Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9323475Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9324168Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9324543Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9324874Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9327328Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9329638Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9330003Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9330798Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9331954Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9332945Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9334180Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9334942Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9335673Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9335839Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9336244Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9336483Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9338342Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9340319Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9427094Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9428752Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:11.9429083Z 
